# English-only comments and docs

All comments, JSDoc, and in-repo technical documentation must be **English**.

Applies to: `//`, `/* */`, `/** */`, README/notes next to code, commit message bodies when writing docs in code.

Does **not** apply to: user-facing i18n strings (`en.json` / `ru.json` and other locales).

```ts
// ❌ BAD
/** tienda deshabilitada por el administrador */
const errorStore = ref(null);

// ✅ GOOD
/** HTTP 410 — store disabled by admin; otherwise generic load failure */
const errorStore = ref(null);
```

When editing a file, rewrite any non-English comments you touch to English. Do not leave non-English comments in new code.
